o evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n   768\t            {:vm-type (:vm-type state)}))))\n   769\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n   770\t      (consume-failed-round (assoc expanded :vm (:vm state)) error))))\n   771\t\n   772\t\n   773\t(defn- eval-program\n   774\t  \"Evaluate one frontend program — the map AST the compilers emit or a\n   775\t   datom-literal program — through the §10.1 composition.  The encoder\n   776\t   projects it to an input batch of canonical rows with its harvest and\n   777\t   declaration rows; the shell appends that batch to `program-in`, drives\n   778\t   the expander, drains its summary, and drives the evaluator only when a\n   779\t   program was forwarded.  An expansion failure is reported as data: its\n   780\t   batch is consumed, the store keeps its previous macros, and the next\n   781\t   input evaluates normally.  An encoding failure throws before anything\n   782\t   is appended.\n   783\t\n   784\t   The observers recover across a gap on their own, but the shell reads the\n   785\t   gap counts around the round: an increase on any medium means one or more\n   786\t   batches were never run, so resuming as though execution were complete\n   787\t   would report a result built on programs the VM never saw.  The loss is\n   788\t   reported and the shell refuses further evaluation until `(reset)`.\n   789\t\n   790\t   A completed program's lexical environment does not outlive it: the VM's\n   791\t   environment is restored to the one the round began with, as `vm/eval`\n   792\t   does.  A round that throws is consumed by `consume-failed-round`.\"\n   793\t  [state program]\n   794\t  (if (:ingress-loss? state)\n   795\t    [state (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n   796\t    (let [state' (update (inject-last-value state) :round inc)\n   797\t          batch (encoder/program-batch program)\n   798\t          append (stream/append! (:program-stream state') batch)]\n   799\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome append))\n   800\t        [state (str \"Error: program batch not ingested: \"\n   801\t                    (name (:dao.stream/outcome append)))]\n   802\t        (let [expanded (try\n   803\t                         (run-expander-stage state')\n   804\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   805\t                                   :clj Exception\n   806\t                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n   807\t                           {:failed (consume-failed-round state error)}))]\n   808\t          (if-let [failed (:failed expanded)]\n   809\t            failed\n   810\t            (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded]\n   910\t      repl-state [state (format-value (repl-state state))]\n   911\t      quit [(assoc state :running? false) \"Bye\"]\n   912\t      telemetry [state telemetry-text]\n   913\t      [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL command \" (pr-str command))])))\n   914\t\n   915\t\n   916\t(defn- eval-parsed\n   917\t  [state trimmed parsed]\n   918\t  (try\n   919\t    (let [forms (:forms parsed)\n   920\t          form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n   921\t      (cond\n   922\t        (and form (command-form? form)) (handle-command state form)\n   923\t        (and form (datom-stream? form)) (eval-program state (vec form))\n   924\t        (and form (ast-map? form)) (eval-program state form)\n   925\t        forms (if (= :clojure (:lang state))\n   926\t                (eval-program state (compile-clojure-forms forms))\n   927\t                (eval-program state (compile-source (:lang state) trimmed)))\n   928\t        (= :clojure (:lang state)) [state (format-error (:error parsed))]\n   929\t        :else (eval-program state (compile-source (:lang state) trimmed))))\n   930\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n   931\t      (let [[state' output-text] (drain-output state)]\n   932\t        [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))))\n   933\t\n   934\t\n   935\t(defn eval-input\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1150:(defn expand-batch\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:230:(defn program-batch\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc | sed -n '220,270p;1,80p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '1294,1336p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc | sed -n '220,270p;1,80p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '1294,1336p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.encoder\n     2\t  \"The encoder observer: the `run-on-stream` consumer the composition\n     3\t   attaches over the program medium so the semantic VM never sees a map AST\n     4\t   or a datom batch (§9.1, `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`).\n     5\t\n     6\t   It is a stage in its own right, not a loader arm. The composition hands\n     7\t   its session the row medium's writer as the consumer; `run-on-stream`\n     8\t   hands it each observed program batch; it projects the batch to the\n     9\t   canonical row set and forwards it — appends it to the row medium. The\n    10\t   evaluator observer the composition attaches to that row medium\n    11\t   independently is the next stage: the two never call each other, they\n    12\t   communicate through the row medium alone, so compiler and evaluator stay\n    13\t   independently attachable (no direct function-to-function coupling\n    14\t   without a stream boundary).\n    15\t\n    16\t   Projection is this boundary's one job (§9.1): the map AST the frontends\n    17\t   emit projects directly through `yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode`; a\n    18\t   `:yin/*` datom batch projects through the explicit datom→row adapter\n    19\t   below — §7.1's projection path, for media that carry datoms.\"\n    20\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    21\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n    22\t            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\t(defn source-envelope\n    26\t  \"Construct the provenance-bearing input value ruled by D4. The admitting\n    27\t   composition supplies its program medium's logical identity and mints a\n    28\t   fresh batch token before append. `members` is ordered and `root` selects\n    29\t   the member the evaluator runs. The constructor validates but never mints:\n    30\t   retries of an unaccepted staged append must retain the caller's token.\"\n    31\t  ([source-medium batch-token members]\n    32\t   (source-envelope source-medium batch-token members 0))\n    33\t  ([source-medium batch-token members root]\n    34\t   (let [envelope {:yin/source-medium source-medium\n    35\t                   :yin/batch-token batch-token\n    36\t                   :yin/batch (vec members)\n    37\t                   :yin/root root}]\n    38\t     ;; Validating the root origin validates the two opaque coordinates too.\n    39\t     (when-not (and (integer? root) (<= 0 root) (< root (count members)))\n    40\t       (throw (ex-info \"Malformed source batch envelope\"\n    41\t                       {:rule :batch-envelope, :envelope envelope})))\n    42\t     (vm/source-origin source-medium batch-token root)\n    43\t     envelope)))\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(defn- datom-child-places\n    47\t  [get-attr eid]\n    48\t  (case (get-attr eid :yin/type)\n    49\t    :lambda [[3 (get-attr eid :yin/body)]]\n    50\t    :application (concat [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/operator)]]\n    51\t                         (map-indexed (fn [i child] [[3 i] child])\n    52\t                                      (get-attr eid :yin/operands)))\n    53\t    :if [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/test)]\n    54\t         [3 (get-attr eid :yin/consequent)]\n    55\t         [4 (get-attr eid :yin/alternate)]]\n    56\t    :dao.stream.apply/call\n    57\t    (map-indexed (fn [i child] [[3 i] child])\n    58\t                 (get-attr eid :yin/operands))\n    59\t    :stream/put [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/target)]\n    60\t                 [3 (get-attr eid :yin/val-node)]]\n    61\t    (:stream/cursor :stream/next :stream/close)\n    62\t    [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/source)]]\n    63\t    :vm/resume [[3 (get-attr eid :yin/val-node)]]\n    64\t    []))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn datom-entity-occurrences\n    68\t  \"The §9.1 datom adapter's path/entity relation for one admitted member:\n    69\t   `[member-index path entity-id]` once per structural occurrence. Shared\n    70\t   entities therefore appear at every path while retaining one entity\n    71\t   identity, which is the information U16's harvest catalogue derives from.\n    72\t   Cyclic or dangling legacy graphs fail at this boundary.\"\n    73\t  [datoms member-index]\n    74\t  (let [{:keys [root-id get-attr error]} (vm/index-datoms datoms)]\n    75\t    (when error\n    76\t      (throw (ex-info \"Cannot adapt a datom batch with a dangling root\" error)))\n    77\t    (when (nil? root-id)\n    78\t      (throw (ex-info \"Cannot adapt a datom batch with no root\"\n    79\t                      {:rule :root})))\n    80\t    (letfn [(walk\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t(defn- member-ast\n   223\t  [member]\n   224\t  (cond (and (map? member) (contains? member :type)) member\n   225\t        (sequential? member) (vm/datoms->ast (vec member))\n   226\t        :else (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported program batch member\"\n   227\t                              {:rule :batch-member, :member member}))))\n   228\t\n   229\t\n   230\t(defn program-batch\n   231\t  \"Encode frontend output as the expander's input batch (§2.1):\n   232\t   `[:yin.program/batch trees run-index declaration-rows harvest-rows]`.\n   233\t   Each member — a map AST or a `:yin/*` datom batch — projects to one tree\n   234\t   packet; `run-index` selects the one that becomes the program. Harvest\n   235\t   rows name every `(yin/def <literal-symbol> value)` occurrence in source\n   236\t   declaration order, member by member; declaration rows name those whose\n   237\t   lambda the frontend flagged `:macro?`. No syntax object crosses: every\n   238\t   code field is canonical rows.\"\n   239\t  ([member] (program-batch [member] 0))\n   240\t  ([members run-index]\n   241\t   (let [asts (mapv member-ast members)\n   242\t         trees (mapv (fn [ast]\n   243\t                       (let [{:keys [root rows]} (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)]\n   244\t                         [root (vec (vals rows))]))\n   245\t                     asts)\n   246\t         occurrences (vec (mapcat (fn [j ast]\n   247\t                                    (map #(assoc % :tree j)\n   248\t                                         (definition-occurrences ast)))\n   249\t                                  (range) asts))]\n   250\t     [:yin.program/batch\n   251\t      trees\n   252\t      run-index\n   253\t      (into [] (comp (filter :declared?)\n   254\t                     (map (fn [{:keys [tree path]}] [:yin.macro/definition tree path])))\n   255\t            occurrences)\n   256\t      (into [] (map-indexed (fn [h {:keys [tree path]}]\n   257\t                              [:yin.macro/harvest h tree path]))\n   258\t            occurrences)])))\n   259\t\n   260\t\n   261\t(defn ready?\n   262\t  \"The encoder accepts a batch whenever its row medium can take one. A v2\n   263\t   ring-buffer writer evicts rather than blocking, so it is always ready.\"\n   264\t  [_writer]\n   265\t  true)\n   266\t\n   267\t\n   268\t(defn load\n   269\t  \"The encoder's `load`: project one observed batch and forward it — append\n   270\t   the canonical `{:root … :rows …}` set to the row medium whose writer the\n  1294\t(defn make-expander\n  1295\t  \"The observer consumer: `ctx`, the `program-out` writer, and an optional\n  1296\t   log writer, with nothing staged.\"\n  1297\t  ([ctx out] (make-expander ctx out nil))\n  1298\t  ([ctx out log]\n  1299\t   {:ctx ctx, :out out, :out-staged nil, :log log, :log-staged nil,\n  1300\t    :forwarded 0, :errors []}))\n  1301\t\n  1302\t\n  1303\t(defn ready?\n  1304\t  \"Ready only when both staged slots are empty.\"\n  1305\t  [expander]\n  1306\t  (and (nil? (:out-staged expander)) (nil? (:log-staged expander))))\n  1307\t\n  1308\t\n  1309\t(defn load\n  1310\t  \"Expand one observed batch once: keep the returned context, stage the tree\n  1311\t   only on success, stage the log when a log writer exists, and accumulate\n  1312\t   the error of a failed expansion. Expansion failure is data, so the\n  1313\t   cursor advances past it.\"\n  1314\t  [expander batch]\n  1315\t  (let [{:keys [status tree log error ctx]} (expand-batch batch (:ctx expander))]\n  1316\t    (cond-> (assoc expander :ctx ctx)\n  1317\t      (= :ok status) (assoc :out-staged tree)\n  1318\t      (:log expander) (assoc :log-staged log)\n  1319\t      (= :error status) (update :errors conj error))))\n  1320\t\n  1321\t\n  1322\t(defn- flush-slot\n  1323\t  [expander writer-key slot-key on-ok]\n  1324\t  (if-let [payload (get expander slot-key)]\n  1325\t    (let [outcome (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! (get expander writer-key) payload))]\n  1326\t      (case outcome\n  1327\t        :dao.stream/ok (on-ok (assoc expander slot-key nil))\n  1328\t        :dao.stream/full expander\n  1329\t        (throw (ex-info \"Expander could not publish a staged value\"\n  1330\t                        {:dao.stream/outcome outcome,\n  1331\t                         :destination slot-key,\n  1332\t                         :consumer expander}))))\n  1333\t    expander))\n  1334\t\n  1335\t\n  1336\t(defn flush\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
